## Error Handling UI Patterns

### 1. Form Error Display

Show errors clearly and contextually:

```typescript
const ErrorDisplay = Shade<{ error: string }>({
  render: ({ props }) => (
    props.error ? (
      <div style={{
        color: 'var(--theme-error-main)',
        fontSize: '14px',
        marginBottom: '16px',
        padding: '8px',
        backgroundColor: 'var(--theme-error-light)',
        borderRadius: '4px',
        border: '1px solid var(--theme-error-main)',
      }}>
        {props.error}
      </div>
    ) : null
  )
})
```

### 2. Global Error Handling

Use notification system for global feedback:

```typescript
const handleAsyncOperation = async () => {
  try {
    await riskyOperation()

    notyService.emit('onNotyAdded', {
      title: 'Success',
      body: 'Operation completed successfully',
      type: 'success',
    })
  } catch (error) {
    notyService.emit('onNotyAdded', {
      title: 'Error',
      body: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Operation failed',
      type: 'error',
    })
  }
}
```

## Accessibility Considerations

### 1. Keyboard Navigation

Ensure components are keyboard accessible:

```typescript
const AccessibleButton = Shade({
  render: ({ props }) => (
    <div
      role="button"
      tabindex="0"
      onclick={props.onClick}
      onkeydown={(e) => {
        if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') {
          e.preventDefault()
          props.onClick?.()
        }
      }}
      style={{ cursor: 'pointer' }}
    >
      {props.children}
    </div>
  )
})
```

### 2. ARIA Labels

Provide proper labels for screen readers:

```typescript
const Avatar = Shade({
  render: ({ props }) => (
    <div
      role="button"
      aria-label={`User menu for ${props.username}`}
      aria-expanded={props.isMenuOpen}
      aria-haspopup="menu"
    >
      {/* Avatar content */}
    </div>
  )
})
```

## Performance Considerations

### 1. Component Lifecycle

Dispose of observables properly:

```typescript
const EfficientComponent = Shade({
  render: ({ useDisposable }) => {
    // useDisposable automatically handles cleanup
    const state = useDisposable('state', () => new ObservableValue(initialValue))

    // Component implementation...
  },
})
```

### 2. Event Handler Optimization

Avoid creating new functions on every render:

```typescript
// ✅ Good - Handler defined once
const Component = Shade({
  render: ({ useDisposable }) => {
    const isOpen = useDisposable('isOpen', () => new ObservableValue(false))

    const handleToggle = () => isOpen.setValue(!isOpen.getValue())

    return <Button onclick={handleToggle}>Toggle</Button>
  }
})
```

This comprehensive set of UI patterns ensures consistent, accessible, and maintainable user interface components throughout the application.
